+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially a switch to email to save the SMS cost.
+Reminders go by SMS because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food. This page records the
+reason after volunteers proposed email three times in one year.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+During the April–June 2025 email trial, the provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never opened.
+Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag whose fresh food went in
+the bin at closing time. Many members share one phone within their family and do not check email; they see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025. By August, missed pickups were back to 6%. In the
+[latest proposal to switch to email](../../notes/issue-52.md), the maintainer confirmed that SMS would remain.
+
+Email was proposed because it is free, while SMS costs €40 per month. The pantry keeps that expense because the
+trial showed that saving on messages came with more missed pickups and wasted food.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The reminder's timing, message and channel selection live in [the reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py).
